    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an AI sentiment analysis assistant for Vanguard Auto Shop. Read the customer's feedback text only. You do not know anything about this customer's past visits — do not guess or assume repeat visits. Just score the message in front of you. Return a strict JSON object with no markdown fences, no extra words, nothing before or after the JSON.\n\nImportant: if the customer describes a specific problem with the service or their visit (a delay, a wait, something not done correctly, damage, etc.), treat the feedback as negative — even if they are also polite about staff or say something positive about the people involved. Praise for staff does not cancel out a stated complaint about the service itself. Only treat feedback as positive if there is no real complaint being described.\n\nRules for Classification:\n1. Positive Feedback (no complaint about the service itself — compliments, satisfaction, no issues mentioned) -> status_suggestion = \"READY_TO_POST\", severity_score = 1 to 2.\n2. Mild Negative Feedback (a specific but minor complaint is mentioned — wait times, slight delays, small annoyance — even if paired with polite or positive comments about staff) -> status_suggestion = \"PRIVATE_QUEUE\", severity_score = 1 to 3.\n3. Severe/Critical Feedback (vehicle damage, safety hazards, rude behavior, legal or financial threats) -> status_suggestion = \"ESCALATED_MANAGER\", severity_score = 4 to 5.\n4. Ambiguous or Unclear Feedback (you genuinely cannot tell if it is positive or negative) -> is_ambiguous = true, status_suggestion = \"FLAGGED_HUMAN_REVIEW\".\n\nOnly write ai_draft_response if the feedback is negative (rule 2 or rule 3). For positive feedback, leave ai_draft_response as an empty string.\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this exact structure:\n{\n  \"sentiment_score\": <number between -10 and 10>,\n  \"severity_score\": <number between 1 and 5>,\n  \"status_suggestion\": \"<READY_TO_POST | PRIVATE_QUEUE | ESCALATED_MANAGER | FLAGGED_HUMAN_REVIEW>\",\n  \"is_ambiguous\": <boolean>,\n  \"ai_draft_response\": \"<A polite, professional response draft suited to the context, or empty string if feedback is positive>\"\n}",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "type": "HumanMessagePromptTemplate",
              "message": "={{ $('INTAKE').item.json.body.submission.questions[3].value }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        992,
        320
      ],
      "id": "9b19771c-84e7-4cc1-91ad-8830f0496307",
      "name": "AI Sentiment"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// 1. Get AI Sentiment output safely\nlet aiData = {};\ntry {\n  aiData = $('AI Sentiment').first()?.json || {};\n} catch (e) {\n  aiData = $input.all()?.[0]?.json || {};\n}\n\n// Clean and extract raw AI response\nconst rawText = aiData.text || aiData.output || aiData.response || aiData.content || \"\";\nconst cleanedText = typeof rawText === 'string' ? rawText.replace(/```json/g, \"\").replace(/```/g, \"\").trim() : \"\";\n\n// Default values\nlet sentimentScore = -2;\nlet severityScore = 2;\nlet aiDraftResponse = \"\";\nlet statusSuggestion = \"PRIVATE_QUEUE\";\nlet isAmbiguous = false;\n\nif (cleanedText) {\n  try {\n    const parsed = JSON.parse(cleanedText);\n    if (parsed.sentiment_score !== undefined) sentimentScore = Number(parsed.sentiment_score);\n    if (parsed.severity_score !== undefined) severityScore = Number(parsed.severity_score);\n    aiDraftResponse = parsed.ai_draft_response || parsed.ai_response || parsed.draft_response || parsed.response || parsed.suggested_reply || \"\";\n    if (parsed.status_suggestion) statusSuggestion = parsed.status_suggestion;\n    if (parsed.is_ambiguous) isAmbiguous = parsed.is_ambiguous;\n  } catch (e) {\n    // fallback to defaults above\n  }\n}\n\n// 2. Get customer info from Resolve Customer ID (works for both new and existing customers)\nlet customerId = null;\nlet hasPreviousNegative = false;\ntry {\n  const customerData = $('Resolve Customer ID').first()?.json || {};\n  customerId = customerData.customer_id || null;\n  hasPreviousNegative = customerData.has_previous_negative === true;\n} catch (e) {\n  customerId = null;\n  hasPreviousNegative = false;\n}\n\n// 3. Repeat customer = based entirely on the database flag now, no keyword guessing\nconst isRepeatCustomer = hasPreviousNegative;\n\n// 4. Routing logic — positive feedback is checked FIRST, so a repeat-negative\n// customer leaving genuinely positive feedback still gets Ready to Post,\n// not escalated by mistake.\nlet finalStatus = \"PRIVATE_QUEUE\";\n\nif (statusSuggestion === \"READY_TO_POST\" && sentimentScore > 2 && !isAmbiguous) {\n  // Rule 1: Genuinely positive feedback always goes here, even for repeat customers\n  finalStatus = \"READY_TO_POST\";\n} else if (isAmbiguous) {\n  // Rule 2: Unclear feedback goes to human review\n  finalStatus = \"FLAGGED_HUMAN_REVIEW\";\n} else if (isRepeatCustomer) {\n  // Rule 3: Not positive, and this customer has a negative history — escalate regardless of this message's severity\n  finalStatus = \"ESCALATED_MANAGER\";\n} else if (severityScore >= 4 || statusSuggestion === \"ESCALATED_MANAGER\") {\n  // Rule 4: First-time but severe feedback also escalates\n  finalStatus = \"ESCALATED_MANAGER\";\n} else {\n  // Rule 5: Everything else (mild negative, first-time) sits in the private queue\n  finalStatus = \"PRIVATE_QUEUE\";\n}\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    customer_id: customerId,\n    sentiment_score: sentimentScore,\n    severity_score: severityScore,\n    ai_draft_response: aiDraftResponse,\n    status: finalStatus,\n    status_suggestion: finalStatus,\n    alert_status: finalStatus === \"ESCALATED_MANAGER\" ? \"OPEN\" : \"RESOLVED\",\n    response_sent: false,\n    is_repeat_customer: isRepeatCustomer,\n    created_at: new Date().toISOString()\n  }\n}];"
      },
